# Equipment and Technology Policy
**Daisy Health**
**Policy ID:** HR-ET-007
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2025
**Last Reviewed:** June 1, 2025
**Owner:** IT and People Operations

---

## Purpose

Daisy Health provides employees with the tools and technology they need to do their best work. This policy outlines how equipment is provisioned, what employees are responsible for, and how to request additional tools or report issues.

---

## Scope

This policy applies to all full-time and part-time Daisy Health employees. Contractors use equipment per their engagement agreements.

---

## 1. Standard Equipment Provisioning

All full-time employees receive the following upon hire:

- **MacBook Pro or equivalent** (model based on role requirements)
- **USB-C hub or dock**
- **Headset** for virtual meetings and clinical encounters
- **Webcam** (if not built into assigned laptop model)

Equipment is shipped to your home address before your start date. If your equipment does not arrive by your first day, contact IT at it@daisyhealth.com immediately.

Part-time employees receive a laptop only. Additional equipment may be requested through the IT Help Portal.

---

## 2. Clinical Staff Equipment

Clinical employees have additional equipment needs to support telehealth encounters:

- **Clinical-grade headset** with noise cancellation
- **Ring light or equivalent lighting** for professional video quality during patient visits
- **Second monitor** upon request and manager approval, for EHR and telehealth platform simultaneous use

Clinical staff should submit equipment requests through the IT Help Portal within their first 7 days.

---

## 3. Equipment Care and Responsibility

Employees are responsible for the care of all company-issued equipment. This includes:

- Keeping equipment in good working condition
- Not modifying, disassembling, or attempting to repair equipment without IT authorization
- Using a protective case for laptops, especially if transported frequently
- Not allowing household members or others to use company equipment
- Reporting damage or malfunction to IT within 24 hours

**Accidental damage** is covered by Daisy Health for the first incident per employee per year. **Negligent damage** (e.g., spills caused by carelessness, drops from unsecured locations) may result in the employee being responsible for repair or replacement costs up to $300.

---

## 4. Software and Application Approval

Only IT-approved software may be installed on company devices. This protects Daisy Health systems from security vulnerabilities and licensing risks.

### Approved Software Categories

- **Productivity:** Microsoft 365 (Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams), Google Workspace
- **Communication:** Slack, Zoom (Daisy Health account only)
- **Clinical:** EHR platform, telehealth platform, e-prescribing tools
- **Security:** VPN client, password manager, endpoint protection (pre-installed)

### Requesting New Software

Submit a software request through the IT Help Portal. IT will review for security and licensing compliance within 5 business days. Do not download or purchase software before receiving IT approval.

### Prohibited Software

The following may not be installed on company devices:

- Personal cloud storage apps (personal Dropbox, Google Drive personal, iCloud)
- Peer-to-peer file sharing software
- Cryptocurrency mining software
- Any software from unverified or unknown sources
- Personal games or entertainment apps

---

## 5. Personal Device Use (BYOD)

Employees who wish to use a personal device for work must:

- Receive written approval from IT
- Enroll the device in Daisy Health's Mobile Device Management (MDM) system
- Accept that IT may remotely wipe the device if it is lost, stolen, or if employment ends
- Never store PHI on a personal device outside of MDM-managed apps

Personal devices may not be used to access the EHR or conduct clinical encounters without IT and Compliance approval.

---

## 6. Equipment Return

When employment ends for any reason, employees must return all company equipment within **5 business days** of their last day. People Operations will provide return shipping instructions.

Equipment that is not returned within 5 business days may result in the value of the equipment being deducted from the employee's final paycheck, to the extent permitted by applicable law.

Employees transferring to a new role within Daisy Health retain their current equipment unless IT determines an upgrade is needed.

---

## 7. Lost or Stolen Equipment

If your equipment is lost or stolen:

1. Report it to IT Security immediately at security@daisyhealth.com
2. File a police report if theft is suspected
3. Notify your manager

IT will remotely wipe the device to protect Daisy Health data and patient PHI. A replacement device will be issued within 3–5 business days. Employees who lose equipment due to negligence may be responsible for a replacement contribution of up to $300.

---

## 8. IT Support

Daisy Health IT support is available Monday through Friday, 8 AM – 8 PM ET.

- **Help Portal:** it.daisyhealth.com
- **Email:** it@daisyhealth.com
- **Urgent issues (clinical downtime):** 1-800-DAISY-IT (24/7 for clinical staff)

Submit all non-urgent requests through the Help Portal to ensure proper tracking and prioritization.

---

## 9. Home Office Stipend

Employees may use the $500 home office stipend (see Expense Reimbursement Policy HR-EX-004) for peripheral equipment not provided by IT, such as a monitor, keyboard, ergonomic chair, or desk accessories. The stipend is separate from IT-provisioned equipment.

